WEBVTT

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:10.390
That way!

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.100
Brat!

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.560
Damn bestado!

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:40.930
Is that all he had?

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:42.290
That's good enough.

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:42.930
Yeah.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:43.870
Let's go.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:44.680
Yeah.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:14.430
<i>I want to be free.</i>

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:23.170
<i>I want to live up in that free sky.</i>

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.640
<i>That's what I wished for.</i>

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:14.400
You look so beautiful, Your Highness!

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.150
You really do!

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.760
Hurry up, we shouldn't keep the prince waiting.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.740
Fana, it would be rude of you to make him wait.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:29.630
Just act as I showed you.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.020
Exactly as I showed you.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:40.700
I heard the prince is going to ask for
Lady Fana's hand in marriage tonight!

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:46.870
Since he has the Levamme Kingdom's backing,
I'm sure the del Moral family will have to accept.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.060
Well, it's still an auspicious event.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:53.530
We are honored to have you here in San Maltilia.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:55.920
You must be quite tired from your long journey.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.770
The trip home may be even longer.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.090
Do you expect the Amatsuvian Army to give you the usual trouble?

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:07.470
Yeah, they really are a stubborn bunch.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.720
They're quite greedy as well.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:13.350
They'll do anything to get their hands on some gold.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:12.520
Excuse us!

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:14.490
Coming through!

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:15.130
Excuse us.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:15.940
Sorry.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:16.560
Pardon.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.740
Welcome to San Maltilia, Prince Carlo!

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:24.530
I am the Commander of the Levamme Kingdom's Eastern Battalion, Domingo Garcia.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.810
Yes, I've heard of you.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.560
That is indeed an honor!

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:33.250
I am so happy that you decided to come all the way out here.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:39.820
Oh, she's here!

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:40.880
Her Highness!

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:42.650
Lady Fana!

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:00.970
Come, Fana. The prince is waiting.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:37.020
Fana, introduce yourself to Prince Carlo.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:41.360
I am pleased to meet you, Prince Carlo.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:50.080
Is this the moment I have been awaiting for so long?

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:53.450
I must thank God for bringing me to you!

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:58.120
Oh, Fana, I can think of innumerable words to describe you,

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:01.630
but before your beauty, they are all meaningless.

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:10.490
Fana, I want you to be by my side until death do us part.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:23.970
I thank you for your kinds words, and gladly accept this honor.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:31.870
Let us make a promise to reflect our happiness onto the world.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.830
However, as we are still at war with Amatsukami,

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.530
the mainland is in disarray.

00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:40.610
Give me one year.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:44.630
I will defeat Amatsukami within one year and end this war!

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:47.550
Please wait until then.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:05.480
In just one year, you will be the
Queen of the Levamme Kingdom.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:07.670
Our family will finally find stability.

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:27.810
It's been a lot more than one year!

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:30.060
The war just keeps on going.

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:34.300
I wonder what will happen to
Your Highness's engagement to Prince Carlo?

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:38.030
Don't worry.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:44.020
There's no way Prince Carlo would forget about his promise.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:47.220
After all, he sends letters here every day.

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:48.770
He really is kind.

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:51.070
He's one-of-a-kind.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:54.530
There aren't many men as honest as him.

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:03.810
All right, you two. It's time for Her Highness to go to bed.

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:04.820
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:12.450
Good night, Your Highness.

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:30.710
Father!

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.440
Father!

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.090
Come with us, Your Highness!

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:39.400
It's the Amatsuvian Air Force!

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:41.720
Father! Father!

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.240
We have to hurry!

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:02.040
Your Highness, are you all right?!

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:03.760
Lady Fana!

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:06.280
Your Highness! Your Highness!

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:08.010
Lady Fana!

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:24.030
Quickly, get outside!

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.510
What did you say?!

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:51.510
What do you mean they were after Lady Fana?

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:59.020
By taking Lady Fana's life, they believed they could diminish the morale of our army!

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:02.500
Then, you mean Lady Fana is still in danger?

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:04.520
Don't worry.

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:06.720
We just received a telegram.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:12.670
Prince Carlo has ordered the Eighth Division Special Fleet to fly here and escort her back to the mainland.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:17.510
Then, Lady Fana will finally be with Prince Carlo?

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:20.990
That long-awaited day has finally come.

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:40.610
Damn it!

00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:55.200
I think I lost him!

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:02.990
What?!

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:20.390
How long are you gonna sleep, Charles?

00:12:20.390 --> 00:12:22.780
Oh, hey, Joaquim.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:27.260
Don't just lie there. The wake-up call was hours ago.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:28.880
Were you having a nightmare?

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:31.250
Shot down again?

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:32.610
Yeah.

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:40.880
That's what you get for going up against a New-Type.

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:44.730
It doesn't matter how good of a pilot you are, you can't beat them.

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:47.120
It's actually a miracle you survived that.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:50.230
Seriously, those things are monsters.

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:55.920
Man, if only Levamme had planes like those...

00:12:57.340 --> 00:12:58.380
Charles?!

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:00.310
Eat later.

00:13:00.310 --> 00:13:02.300
Go wash these right now.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.400
And do it carefully.

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:08.230
We're not here to do your chores.

00:13:08.230 --> 00:13:10.300
What was that, you mercenary scum?

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:14.530
Why do you hang around with that bestado?

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:17.560
It's okay, Joaquim.

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:18.800
But!

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:21.460
It's okay, I'm used to it.

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:25.070
I'm glad you know your place well!

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:26.700
Keep your head down, damn bestado.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:28.550
What the hell did you say?!

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:29.930
Let it go, Joaquim.

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:31.680
Get 'em, Joaquim!

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:34.030
1st-Rank Pilot Karino!

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.790
Is the 1st-Rank Pilot Charles Karino here?

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:42.100
Yes, sir, I'm here.

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:43.760
We have something urgent to discuss.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.260
Come to the command office.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:46.200
Yes, sir!

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:51.090
Who wants <i>that guy at the command office?</i>

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:56.350
1st-Rank Pilot Charles Karino...

00:13:56.350 --> 00:14:01.260
Father: Levammian, Mother: Amatsuvian.

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:02.910
A bestado, huh?

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:04.070
Yes, sir.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:09.950
So you were a poor street rat from birth, huh?

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:12.450
How did you get by?

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:14.580
Stealing? Begging?

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:19.330
When I was seven, I came to the
Almeria Airfield for informal work.

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:22.220
Where did you learn how to fly?

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:24.910
I found out by watching others.

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:27.870
So, you stole with your eyes?

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:30.590
You really are a rat.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:36.270
However, during simulated dogfights, he bested the regular division's ace.

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:40.440
He is, in both name and reality, San Maltilia's top pilot.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:41.750
I see.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:46.730
There is a very important mission I want to entrust you with.

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:47.990
Yes, sir!

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:52.490
You will escort a member of the Royal Family in a seaplane,

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:56.090
and fly solo to the mainland.

00:14:56.090 --> 00:14:57.840
You will have no guard, of course.

00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:58.850
Can you do it?

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:03.340
It will be difficult to break through the enemy's lines, but not impossible.

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:06.240
Have you flown across the Central Ocean before?

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:07.030
No, sir.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.380
I thought not.

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:11.400
Lieutenant.

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:12.140
Yes, sir.

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:25.640
Where will you fly?

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:35.030
The distance to the mainland is about 12,000 kilometers.

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:38.310
If I am to fly this distance in a seaplane,

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:43.660
I would need to make three stops to recharge the battery.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:45.920
Any obstacles?

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:50.510
The biggest obstacle will be here, the Great Falls.

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:53.880
If I can break through the enemy's patrol fleets there,

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:57.440
I should be able to reach the mainland without issue.

00:15:57.440 --> 00:16:00.200
However, the real problem is the New-Type.

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:06.570
If they deploy the New-Type, it will be
very difficult to escape in the open sea.

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:11.200
For this mission, you will fly our latest
reconnaissance model, the Santa Cruz.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.900
The Santa Cruz?

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:20.220
None of our other models can compare to its mobility.

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:22.890
It can reach speeds of 620 km/h.

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:24.920
It's still not as fast as the New-Type,

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:28.720
but it is certainly within a class of its own.

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:31.610
Anything else?

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:32.740
Just one more, sir.

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:36.430
We will most likely run into enemy patrol planes as soon as we take off,

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:39.970
so it will be a little difficult to evade them.

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:41.360
That's not an issue.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:44.730
Our entire fleet here at San Maltilia will act as a decoy.

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:47.150
What? The entire fleet?

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:47.150
Anything else?

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.730
No, sir!

00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:53.230
Very well.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:17:00.620
Your mission is to escort the next queen, Fana del Moral.

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:07.750
You will take Her Highness to her future husband, Prince Carlo.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:15.260
With all due respect, I believe the Eighth Division
Special Fleet would be better suited for this mission.

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:21.270
The Eighth Division Special Fleet was annihilated at the Great Falls.

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:27.730
If word gets out that the entire fleet was destroyed,

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:30.630
the honor of the Levammian Royal Family will be tarnished.

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:35.550
All of our peace talks will be trodden on as others will call for the war to continue!

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:38.950
That's why we must act!

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:41.000
And that's where you fit in!

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:43.720
You will protect Her Highness and fly across the ocean!

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.080
Then, you will hand her over to a friendly airship,

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:50.340
which, as the sole survivor of the Special Fleet, will return her to the capital!

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:53.690
Can you do it?

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:09.000
I will do all I can to succeed! I accept this mission!

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:10.730
Good.

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:12.080
Stand by for orders.

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:12.920
Yes, sir!

00:18:23.270 --> 00:18:27.390
To think a bestado is tasked to protect our next queen...

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:28.950
It's a sad day.

00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:36.030
Way to go, Charles!

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:38.470
You really are something!

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:41.220
I bet those regular soldiers are ticked off!

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:42.470
Serves them right!

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:46.870
Come on, Charles, why are you so down?

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:48.080
Nervous?

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:49.390
No, it's not that.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:51.830
Don't worry! If anyone can do it, you can.

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:53.480
You probably won't even have to fight!

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:56.250
There aren't any enemies out there.

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:59.240
Besides, we'll be acting as decoys.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:02.070
I'm sorry about that...

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:03.260
Don't worry about it!

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:04.990
Being decoys can be fun!

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:07.090
Yeah, don't worry about us.

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:10.370
We mercenaries are more resilient than cockroaches!

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:13.750
You better drop Her Highness off and come back in one piece!

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:17.280
I will, I promise.

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:19.260
All right, boys!

00:19:19.750 --> 00:19:22.290
No one go off and die, okay?!

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:26.520
Let's all pull this mission off and come back home!

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:28.270
Yeah!

00:19:51.110 --> 00:19:53.180
Now then, I will lay out the plan!

00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:55.720
The Air Specialists Unit will sortie right away.

00:19:55.720 --> 00:20:00.660
The Direct Line and Bomber Units will follow 15 minutes later!

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:05.200
You will all act as decoys for the next Queen of Levamme, Fana del Moral!

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:08.560
You must draw all of the enemy's fighters away from San Maltilia!

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:11.740
Do not let up the attack for even a second!

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:14.460
Show them the pride of the Levammian Army!

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:17.550
Now, prepare yourselves for sortie!

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:18.460
Yes, sir!

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:21.170
Karino, come with me.

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:22.450
Yes, sir!

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:23.770
Good luck!

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:25.120
Count on us decoys!

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:26.040
Yeah.

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:34.970
Under normal circumstances, you would never be allowed to see even her face.

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:36.630
Don't make any pointless chatter.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:38.920
Answer all questions with "yes" or "no".

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:41.470
I don't want her to be tainted by a street rat like yourself.

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:42.850
Are we clear?

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:43.790
Yes, sir.

00:21:02.620 --> 00:21:04.870
Forgive us for making you wait.

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:10.380
This is the man we have chosen for this mission, 1st-Rank Pilot Karino.

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:39.290
He looks a little young, doesn't he?

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:41.360
You have nothing to worry about.

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:43.950
He is our army's finest pilot.

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:49.280
Even amongst a group of skillful pilots, he stands out.

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:52.540
If you're interested, look near your feet.

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:54.370
I left something for you.

00:21:55.530 --> 00:21:56.540
We're counting on you.

00:22:41.920 --> 00:22:43.620
We can't fit all of these!

00:22:43.620 --> 00:22:44.910
Don't be ridiculous!

00:22:44.910 --> 00:22:48.160
There's no way you can't fit these in! It's nothing!

00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:51.450
But, the more weight the plane carries, the slower it flies!

00:22:51.450 --> 00:22:54.760
That's why we only brought what she absolutely needed!

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:56.180
She needs all of this?!

00:22:57.420 --> 00:22:59.590
Yes, Lady Fana needs all of this!

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:01.170
We won't remove anything!

00:23:01.170 --> 00:23:03.270
Now, put them in!

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:04.580
But...

00:23:11.440 --> 00:23:15.120
Okay, we'll pack them right away.

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:16.830
You better!

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:18.680
What a nuisance!

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:35.050
Careful.

00:23:37.460 --> 00:23:38.580
Right here.

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:43.390
Please watch your step.

00:23:50.550 --> 00:23:52.970
Well then, take care.

00:23:58.970 --> 00:24:02.180
You understand failure isn't an option, right, Karino?

00:24:02.180 --> 00:24:03.090
Yes, sir.

00:24:03.090 --> 00:24:04.600
I will give it my all.

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:08.800
Engine starting. Clear in front!

00:24:28.690 --> 00:24:31.780
Can you hear me, Your Highness?

00:24:33.830 --> 00:24:35.260
Yes.

00:24:35.260 --> 00:24:36.890
We're about to take off.

00:24:36.890 --> 00:24:37.850
Okay.

00:24:38.690 --> 00:24:40.340
Your Highness!

00:24:40.340 --> 00:24:42.570
Take care, Your Highness!

00:24:42.570 --> 00:24:45.080
We'll pray for your safety!

00:24:51.770 --> 00:24:54.540
Your Highness!

00:25:07.860 --> 00:25:09.650
Preparations complete, Santa Cruz.

00:25:09.650 --> 00:25:12.320
Cleared for take off.

00:25:12.340 --> 00:25:13.330
Roger.

00:25:30.780 --> 00:25:31.840
Let's go.

00:26:13.710 --> 00:26:15.170
That should be high enough.

00:26:16.420 --> 00:26:20.010
Your Highness, it would help if you kept a look-out for any enemies.

00:26:21.300 --> 00:26:21.930
Okay.

00:26:21.930 --> 00:26:25.410
Thank you, please keep watch behind us.

00:26:25.410 --> 00:26:26.600
Okay.

00:28:40.080 --> 00:28:42.360
We'll rest here for tonight.

00:28:42.360 --> 00:28:44.530
Also, I have a request.

00:28:54.120 --> 00:28:57.040
Please throw away anything you don't absolutely need.

00:29:09.070 --> 00:29:12.450
The Santa Cruz is a very fast plane.

00:29:12.450 --> 00:29:16.570
But, no matter how fast a plane is, if it's carrying extra weight,

00:29:16.570 --> 00:29:19.580
it will lose velocity and be shot down by the enemy.

00:29:20.550 --> 00:29:22.370
Oh, I see.

00:29:22.370 --> 00:29:23.560
I understand.

00:29:23.560 --> 00:29:26.180
Then, please.

00:29:26.180 --> 00:29:27.190
Okay.

00:29:49.800 --> 00:29:51.580
Your Highness!

00:29:51.580 --> 00:29:52.790
I'm here!

00:30:20.810 --> 00:30:21.900
Are you all right?

00:30:25.180 --> 00:30:27.970
I'm sorry I fell off.

00:30:29.180 --> 00:30:30.810
Please be more careful.

00:30:38.230 --> 00:30:40.730
It's an enemy fleet! It's coming this way!

00:30:41.400 --> 00:30:43.570
Please get inside, we're taking off!

00:30:47.670 --> 00:30:49.740
Forget your luggage! Hurry!

00:30:49.740 --> 00:30:50.680
Okay!

00:31:21.050 --> 00:31:23.370
It looks like they didn't see us.

00:31:23.360 --> 00:31:24.400
Yes.

00:31:30.950 --> 00:31:33.830
This plane recharges by filling its tank with ocean water.

00:31:33.830 --> 00:31:36.330
It takes one night to fully recharge.

00:31:36.330 --> 00:31:40.670
We'll have enough in the tank to last for all of tomorrow's flight.

00:31:49.460 --> 00:31:52.300
I guess we should change into some new clothes.

00:31:52.300 --> 00:31:54.230
I don't have any others.

00:31:54.220 --> 00:31:56.720
All of my bags fell into the ocean.

00:31:59.210 --> 00:32:00.770
Oh...

00:32:14.200 --> 00:32:15.530
I'm...

00:32:15.530 --> 00:32:19.310
I'm sorry for causing you so much trouble.

00:32:19.310 --> 00:32:21.580
You haven't.

00:32:32.120 --> 00:32:34.540
Well, I'm going to get some sleep.

00:32:36.370 --> 00:32:37.480
Um...

00:32:37.480 --> 00:32:38.590
Yes?

00:32:38.590 --> 00:32:41.700
Where will you sleep, Mr. Pilot?

00:32:41.700 --> 00:32:42.810
Inside the plane.

00:32:43.770 --> 00:32:45.310
Isn't that too small?

00:32:45.310 --> 00:32:46.760
I'm used to it.

00:32:46.770 --> 00:32:49.360
I sleep fine even on my cramped bed.

00:32:50.190 --> 00:32:52.860
When you go to sleep, please turn off the burner.

00:32:52.860 --> 00:32:53.770
Okay.

00:33:45.740 --> 00:33:47.270
That song...

00:34:33.090 --> 00:34:34.670
Okay, let's head out.

00:34:34.670 --> 00:34:37.090
Please keep watch behind us again.

00:34:37.090 --> 00:34:38.150
Okay.

00:35:32.690 --> 00:35:36.690
I can see a light in the clouds on our upper-right side!

00:35:38.690 --> 00:35:41.230
I don't see anything.

00:35:41.230 --> 00:35:44.190
I saw it within that large cloud.

00:35:49.050 --> 00:35:50.580
You were right!

00:35:50.580 --> 00:35:52.260
It's an enemy fleet.

00:36:03.220 --> 00:36:05.770
I don't think they saw us, they're getting further away.

00:36:05.770 --> 00:36:07.300
Thanks for spotting them.

00:36:07.300 --> 00:36:08.980
Good job.

00:36:08.980 --> 00:36:13.000
But why are there fleets out here?

00:36:12.980 --> 00:36:15.150
And last night, too.

00:36:15.150 --> 00:36:17.170
Do they know where we're flying?

00:36:17.170 --> 00:36:20.160
What if they do know?

00:36:20.160 --> 00:36:22.800
If Amatsukami found out about our plan,

00:36:22.800 --> 00:36:26.680
they would immediately send out waves of their New-Type fighter planes.

00:36:26.680 --> 00:36:30.680
If it comes to that, we would have no chance of surviving.

00:36:30.680 --> 00:36:33.660
This plane's firepower consists of that gun in the rear.

00:36:33.660 --> 00:36:36.380
Do you know how to use it?

00:36:36.380 --> 00:36:38.060
No.

00:36:38.050 --> 00:36:40.380
Our odds keep getting slimmer, don't they?

00:36:42.160 --> 00:36:44.480
This mission is completely secret.

00:36:44.480 --> 00:36:47.190
The army has taken every precautionary measure.

00:36:47.180 --> 00:36:51.770
There's no way our mission would be leaked out, even by accident.

00:37:00.180 --> 00:37:02.330
If we keep up this pace,

00:37:02.330 --> 00:37:05.410
we should reach Scion Island the day after tomorrow.

00:37:05.410 --> 00:37:08.300
We're not going straight to the capital?

00:37:08.280 --> 00:37:14.830
My mission is to take you to Scion Island, where an airship will be waiting.

00:37:15.880 --> 00:37:22.880
That airship will return triumphantly as the sole
surviving member of the Eighth Division Special Fleet.

00:37:24.740 --> 00:37:28.100
That's a lie, isn't it?

00:37:29.060 --> 00:37:32.300
Are you okay with that, Mr. Pilot?

00:37:32.300 --> 00:37:34.860
They'll take credit for your hard work.

00:37:36.270 --> 00:37:38.860
They'll pay me quite a bit in return.

00:37:39.680 --> 00:37:45.650
For us mercenaries, even if we worked our whole lives we'd never make that much.

00:37:45.660 --> 00:37:48.950
I'll have enough money to fully enjoy my life.

00:37:48.950 --> 00:37:51.800
After this mission, I'll stop being a mercenary,

00:37:51.790 --> 00:37:55.330
and live comfortably on an island somewhere.

00:37:55.330 --> 00:37:57.630
I see.

00:38:12.830 --> 00:38:13.950
Is it the enemy?

00:38:13.950 --> 00:38:14.320
Yes.

00:38:15.480 --> 00:38:18.060
It's okay, they're not coming this way.

00:38:22.140 --> 00:38:24.340
They're searching for something.

00:38:24.340 --> 00:38:26.660
Something's not right after all.

00:38:32.340 --> 00:38:34.490
Um, Mr. Pilot...

00:38:34.490 --> 00:38:35.690
Yes?

00:38:35.710 --> 00:38:40.000
Do you think the Amatsuvian Army managed to intercept a coded telegram?

00:38:40.830 --> 00:38:43.300
No, that doesn't seem very likely.

00:38:43.300 --> 00:38:46.410
Our army wouldn't make such a silly mistake.

00:38:48.210 --> 00:38:51.590
Prince Carlo sent me a letter.

00:38:51.600 --> 00:38:52.350
A letter?

00:38:54.210 --> 00:38:58.480
In it, he said he was upset that a member of the Royal Family

00:38:58.480 --> 00:39:02.690
had to be crammed into a tiny reconnaissance plane

00:39:02.690 --> 00:39:07.520
and sent on a trip across the Central Ocean without a guard.

00:39:07.520 --> 00:39:08.830
He has a point.

00:39:08.820 --> 00:39:11.620
But, that letter...

00:39:13.290 --> 00:39:16.380
was sent through the military's radio telegraph.

00:39:16.900 --> 00:39:17.960
What?!

00:39:17.960 --> 00:39:19.740
Is that bad?

00:39:23.960 --> 00:39:25.140
Mr. Pilot?

00:39:27.800 --> 00:39:29.630
Has our mission been compromised?

00:39:29.630 --> 00:39:33.550
Dozens of our planes left yesterday to act as decoys.

00:39:33.550 --> 00:39:37.410
They led a head-on attack into the midst of the enemy.

00:39:36.850 --> 00:39:38.810
Um...

00:39:37.390 --> 00:39:39.640
Doesn't the prince understand?

00:39:45.660 --> 00:39:48.130
He was just worried about me.

00:39:48.110 --> 00:39:52.410
So he was only worried about his bride-to-be? Did he not care about us soldiers at all?!

00:39:52.410 --> 00:39:55.020
No, that's not...

00:39:55.030 --> 00:39:59.460
The prince just wanted to reach me in the fastest way.

00:39:59.460 --> 00:40:02.400
Doesn't he know that not everyone can be trusted?!

00:40:02.400 --> 00:40:06.080
Did he forget that telegrams can be deciphered?!

00:40:33.580 --> 00:40:36.660
Still, this doesn't mean our mission is over.

00:40:36.660 --> 00:40:39.180
We still have a chance.

00:40:40.000 --> 00:40:44.080
Your Highness has an eye for spotting planes. You proved that today.

00:40:44.080 --> 00:40:45.180
I don't...

00:40:45.900 --> 00:40:48.910
If you spot the enemy before they spot us, we can escape.

00:40:48.910 --> 00:40:51.600
If you can just do that, I'm sure we'll make it through.

00:40:52.590 --> 00:40:54.440
You really think I can be of use?

00:40:54.430 --> 00:40:56.430
I'm counting on you!

00:40:56.430 --> 00:40:58.020
Okay!

00:40:59.990 --> 00:41:01.550
Let's get some sleep.

00:41:01.550 --> 00:41:03.010
Okay.

00:41:03.010 --> 00:41:06.090
Please forgive me for what I said earlier.

00:41:06.090 --> 00:41:07.200
It's okay.

00:41:10.140 --> 00:41:12.140
Well then, good night.

00:41:12.140 --> 00:41:13.650
Good night.

00:41:25.820 --> 00:41:27.170
Um...

00:41:27.170 --> 00:41:28.580
Mr. Pilot?

00:41:35.050 --> 00:41:36.850
Your Highness!

00:41:43.420 --> 00:41:46.500
What were you thinking?

00:41:46.500 --> 00:41:47.960
I'm sorry.

00:41:47.940 --> 00:41:51.440
I just thought you should sleep in a better spot.

00:41:52.280 --> 00:41:55.450
Your body needs a good sleep to recuperate.

00:41:56.970 --> 00:41:59.440
I'm used to it, really.

00:41:59.450 --> 00:42:05.140
Besides, since someone keeps falling into the water, it's better I'm not sound asleep.

00:42:10.230 --> 00:42:15.490
From my manor's window, I could see the sparkling, blue ocean.

00:42:15.490 --> 00:42:21.290
It made me happy, and I always wished I could go see it some day.

00:42:23.980 --> 00:42:26.990
I never thought I'd see it in this manner.

00:42:26.990 --> 00:42:30.770
I think you've been doing more drowning than seeing.

00:42:30.770 --> 00:42:33.040
Oh, yes...

00:42:50.290 --> 00:42:52.130
It's strange.

00:42:52.130 --> 00:42:56.350
I get the feeling this isn't the first time we've met.

00:42:56.350 --> 00:42:58.170
I wonder why.

00:43:14.820 --> 00:43:20.110
<i>Why do we have to work with some filthy bestado?</i>

00:43:20.110 --> 00:43:25.330
<i>I don't know how you and your mother got jobs here.</i>

00:43:25.330 --> 00:43:28.330
<i>Maybe Her Highness took pity on you.</i>

00:43:28.330 --> 00:43:33.380
<i>I wish they'd kick that filthy street rat out of the manor!</i>

00:43:49.470 --> 00:43:50.610
<i>What's wrong?</i>

00:43:51.370 --> 00:43:53.920
<i>You work in the garden, right?</i>

00:43:55.500 --> 00:43:56.630
<i>Are you crying?</i>

00:43:56.630 --> 00:44:00.610
<i>Did something bad happen?</i>

00:44:00.610 --> 00:44:03.170
<i>Nothing happened. I'm not crying!</i>

00:44:27.990 --> 00:44:31.570
<i>You know, flowers bloom by facing the sky.</i>

00:44:31.570 --> 00:44:34.160
<i>Because they're always stuck in the soil,</i>

00:44:34.160 --> 00:44:38.060
<i>they look up towards the wide, free sky.</i>

00:44:38.720 --> 00:44:40.970
<i>Wide and free?</i>

00:44:40.970 --> 00:44:43.420
<i>That's what Chise told me.</i>

00:44:43.420 --> 00:44:44.580
<i>Lady Fana!</i>

00:44:44.580 --> 00:44:46.430
<i>Where are you, Lady Fana?</i>

00:44:47.220 --> 00:44:48.330
<i>Your Highness!</i>

00:44:48.330 --> 00:44:50.770
<i>Sorry, I have to go.</i>

00:45:11.260 --> 00:45:12.420
Mr. Pilot?

00:45:38.130 --> 00:45:41.170
Mr. Pi-l-ot...

00:46:04.640 --> 00:46:06.710
We'll reach the Great Falls today.

00:46:07.350 --> 00:46:09.850
It's the most heavily-guarded enemy location.

00:46:09.850 --> 00:46:12.710
Please keep your eyes sharp.

00:46:12.710 --> 00:46:13.700
Okay!

00:46:31.230 --> 00:46:31.740
Huh?

00:46:32.930 --> 00:46:33.870
What is it?

00:46:33.850 --> 00:46:38.100
Usually, I see patches of blue in between the clouds.

00:46:38.100 --> 00:46:39.520
But?

00:46:39.520 --> 00:46:43.370
But this time, the crack between the one we just passed was completely black.

00:47:05.100 --> 00:47:06.380
Damn it!

00:47:14.400 --> 00:47:16.060
We're surrounded.

00:47:16.060 --> 00:47:18.260
They knew about our mission.

00:47:41.210 --> 00:47:42.870
There are missiles behind us!

00:47:42.870 --> 00:47:44.200
Don't worry about looking around!

00:47:44.210 --> 00:47:45.960
And try not to talk, you'll bite your tongue!

00:48:06.820 --> 00:48:08.030
They're above us!

00:48:08.030 --> 00:48:09.680
Keep your head down!

00:48:44.980 --> 00:48:45.700
I'm sorry.

00:49:26.880 --> 00:49:27.690
Mr. Pilot?

00:49:32.510 --> 00:49:33.670
Mr. Pilot!

00:49:34.070 --> 00:49:34.950
Mr. Pilot!

00:49:39.290 --> 00:49:41.390
The New-Type...

00:49:48.030 --> 00:49:49.370
Mr. Pilot!

00:49:55.090 --> 00:49:57.590
Mr. Pilot! Mr. Pilot!

00:50:00.930 --> 00:50:02.970
Snap out of it, Mr. Pilot!

00:50:26.030 --> 00:50:28.520
Please forgive me, God!

00:50:29.160 --> 00:50:30.230
What?!

00:50:31.040 --> 00:50:32.600
Why?!

00:50:46.670 --> 00:50:47.950
Mr. Pilot!

00:50:47.950 --> 00:50:50.250
Over-boost, huh?

00:50:50.230 --> 00:50:51.110
Damn brat.

00:51:07.630 --> 00:51:09.160
I'm so sorry...

00:51:09.160 --> 00:51:11.550
I can't do anything.

00:51:13.870 --> 00:51:16.910
Fana, I will protect you.

00:51:20.220 --> 00:51:21.990
Keep talking to me.

00:51:21.970 --> 00:51:26.220
I may lose consciousness otherwise.

00:51:27.280 --> 00:51:28.710
Do your best!

00:51:28.710 --> 00:51:30.040
Once this mission is over,

00:51:30.040 --> 00:51:32.220
you'll receive your reward and can go live out your dream!

00:51:34.190 --> 00:51:38.210
No, it's not about the reward.

00:51:39.280 --> 00:51:41.520
Then what?

00:51:41.520 --> 00:51:44.490
My mission this time was to protect someone's life.

00:51:44.490 --> 00:51:48.210
In the past, it had always been to kill the enemy.

00:51:48.850 --> 00:51:54.210
Just once, I wanted to do a mission I could be proud of.

00:52:03.370 --> 00:52:06.280
I'm surprised he's gotten this far in a Levammian plane.

00:52:06.280 --> 00:52:07.720
He's some pilot.

00:52:14.210 --> 00:52:16.260
Damn it! Why can't we hit them?!

00:52:16.260 --> 00:52:17.620
New-Type Division Six!

00:52:17.610 --> 00:52:20.320
If you go any further you'll be too far from the main ship.

00:52:20.320 --> 00:52:21.320
Retreat!

00:52:21.320 --> 00:52:24.200
How can we retreat after chasing them this far?

00:52:28.110 --> 00:52:30.500
You can do it, Mr. Pilot!

00:52:31.370 --> 00:52:32.720
I love it.

00:52:33.440 --> 00:52:36.550
I really love flying.

00:52:37.960 --> 00:52:42.820
Up here, in the sky, your background doesn't matter.

00:52:42.820 --> 00:52:43.980
You're free.

00:52:53.480 --> 00:52:54.860
Shit!

00:52:54.860 --> 00:52:56.670
That's enough, let's head back.

00:52:56.670 --> 00:52:58.420
But, Lieutenant Chijiwa...

00:52:58.420 --> 00:52:59.760
We're retreating.

00:53:02.990 --> 00:53:03.910
Damn it!

00:53:09.110 --> 00:53:10.410
The enemy...

00:53:15.240 --> 00:53:17.040
They stopped chasing us.

00:53:52.540 --> 00:53:54.760
We're going to crash, Mr. Pilot!

00:54:09.550 --> 00:54:10.890
Hang in there!

00:54:53.340 --> 00:54:54.650
We passed the falls!

00:54:55.440 --> 00:54:57.660
We're almost there.

00:54:57.660 --> 00:55:00.430
You can do it, Mr. Pilot!

00:55:00.430 --> 00:55:01.790
Stay with me!

00:55:35.580 --> 00:55:36.430
Mr. Pilot!

00:56:51.550 --> 00:56:53.180
Mr. Pilot...

00:57:36.970 --> 00:57:38.430
Mr. Pilot...

00:57:43.840 --> 00:57:47.640
<i>Stay within the reach of tranquility</i>

00:57:47.640 --> 00:57:53.320
<i>Until your sadness fades away.</i>

00:57:53.320 --> 00:57:59.220
<i>Close your eyes for just a moment,</i>

00:57:59.220 --> 00:58:05.640
<i>And give yourself to me.</i>

00:58:07.710 --> 00:58:13.610
<i>And then, after opening your eyes,</i>

00:58:13.610 --> 00:58:19.930
<i>Temptation will lie before you.</i>

00:58:19.930 --> 00:58:26.350
<i>Once you grasp tomorrow in your hands,</i>

00:58:26.350 --> 00:58:33.210
<i>Temptation will lie before you.</i>

00:59:02.960 --> 00:59:04.070
Ow...

00:59:13.970 --> 00:59:15.950
Good morning, Mr. Pilot.

00:59:20.610 --> 00:59:21.970
How do you feel?

00:59:24.960 --> 00:59:26.910
Your Highness!

00:59:26.910 --> 00:59:28.340
Your hair...

00:59:28.340 --> 00:59:31.970
Oh, it was a bit too long, so I cut it.

00:59:32.660 --> 00:59:33.840
Does it look nice?

00:59:35.470 --> 00:59:36.630
Yes.

00:59:53.300 --> 00:59:54.800
What are you doing?

00:59:57.900 --> 01:00:00.110
It went through a lot yesterday.

01:00:00.110 --> 01:00:03.320
I'll have to move it somewhere to repair it.

01:00:03.320 --> 01:00:05.870
Let me help, too!

01:00:05.870 --> 01:00:07.620
What do you mean?

01:00:07.620 --> 01:00:11.890
Did you think I could just sit back and let someone who's injured do all the work?

01:01:56.690 --> 01:01:58.240
It's beautiful!

01:02:47.200 --> 01:02:48.500
That song...

01:02:49.820 --> 01:02:55.200
My maid from when I was young taught it to me.

01:02:55.200 --> 01:02:57.420
It's a really wonderful song.

01:03:01.790 --> 01:03:05.980
When I was young, I used to listen to that song before falling to sleep.

01:03:05.980 --> 01:03:11.510
My mother and I used to work for the del Moral family.

01:03:11.510 --> 01:03:16.400
I worked in the inner garden, while my mother worked as a maid in the manor.

01:03:17.810 --> 01:03:19.390
No...

01:03:19.400 --> 01:03:21.730
Was Chise your...

01:03:24.150 --> 01:03:28.100
Yes, I'm Chise Karino's son, Charles Karino.

01:03:31.990 --> 01:03:35.750
So, you still remember what my mother told you?

01:03:35.750 --> 01:03:37.730
I'll never forget.

01:03:41.540 --> 01:03:45.090
When I was young, I had trouble
sleeping because I was afraid of the dark.

01:03:47.730 --> 01:03:52.320
I was afraid my mom would come in and scold me.

01:03:53.040 --> 01:03:58.000
But then, Chise would secretly slip in.

01:03:58.670 --> 01:04:04.990
<i>Stay within the warmth's embrace</i>

01:04:04.990 --> 01:04:11.430
<i>Until your sadness fades away.</i>

01:04:11.430 --> 01:04:17.850
<i>Close your eyes for just a moment,</i>

01:04:17.830 --> 01:04:22.330
<i>And give yourself to-</i>

01:04:24.220 --> 01:04:27.210
But one night, my father found out.

01:04:27.950 --> 01:04:30.220
<i>I want you out of here right now!</i>

01:04:31.720 --> 01:04:34.140
Because of me, Chise...

01:04:34.860 --> 01:04:37.430
My mother never forgot you either.

01:04:37.430 --> 01:04:41.130
She would always tell me about Your Highness.

01:04:42.660 --> 01:04:45.150
Is she doing well?

01:04:48.910 --> 01:04:52.410
She passed away soon after leaving the manor.

01:04:57.940 --> 01:04:59.770
Your mother...

01:05:01.180 --> 01:05:03.770
showed me what it meant to be kind.

01:05:03.770 --> 01:05:05.790
Chise...

01:05:05.790 --> 01:05:07.590
I want to see her again!

01:05:11.570 --> 01:05:16.530
I'm sure my mother is smiling from up above after hearing you say that.

01:05:16.530 --> 01:05:19.170
You don't have to cry.

01:05:19.170 --> 01:05:22.530
Save your tears for when you reach the capital.

01:05:28.600 --> 01:05:30.530
I don't want to go to the capital.

01:05:31.240 --> 01:05:33.810
I don't care about my family's status anymore,

01:05:33.810 --> 01:05:35.420
I just want to fly in the sky forever!

01:05:35.420 --> 01:05:38.680
You said you wanted to live out your life on an island somewhere, right?

01:05:39.140 --> 01:05:41.020
Take me with you!

01:05:41.020 --> 01:05:41.610
I...

01:05:41.610 --> 01:05:42.630
Your Highness!

01:05:47.290 --> 01:05:48.970
I can't.

01:05:48.970 --> 01:05:53.860
Everyone's wish is for me to take you to the capital.

01:05:53.860 --> 01:05:58.150
What about my wish?

01:06:07.810 --> 01:06:08.860
Don't do that!

01:06:13.040 --> 01:06:15.160
Okay, give me the bottle.

01:06:15.160 --> 01:06:15.810
No!

01:06:17.730 --> 01:06:19.090
Please, stop!

01:06:19.090 --> 01:06:22.200
You'll feel sick during our flight tomorrow!

01:06:23.900 --> 01:06:25.560
What's it to you?

01:06:25.560 --> 01:06:27.950
I'll drink whatever I want to!

01:06:27.950 --> 01:06:28.720
Coward!

01:06:30.050 --> 01:06:32.720
How am I a coward?

01:06:32.720 --> 01:06:34.070
You just are!

01:06:34.070 --> 01:06:36.590
Yesterday, you said one's background doesn't matter.

01:06:36.590 --> 01:06:38.840
Now today, you've completely changed your attitude!

01:06:38.840 --> 01:06:40.720
That's because...

01:06:40.720 --> 01:06:43.260
You big idiot!

01:06:43.260 --> 01:06:47.130
If you stood next to Prince Carlo, there would be no comparison!

01:06:47.140 --> 01:06:50.520
He's handsome, honest, and...

01:06:50.520 --> 01:06:51.820
Handsome!

01:06:51.820 --> 01:06:53.920
Stop joking around, Your Highness.

01:06:53.920 --> 01:06:57.030
I'm not joking! I'm always serious!

01:07:02.120 --> 01:07:04.040
Fine! Dance with me!

01:07:06.140 --> 01:07:07.830
Where did that come from?

01:07:09.430 --> 01:07:11.180
I can't.

01:07:11.180 --> 01:07:12.590
And why not?

01:07:12.590 --> 01:07:14.560
I'm not a noble.

01:07:14.550 --> 01:07:16.550
I never learned how to dance.

01:07:21.050 --> 01:07:23.520
All right then, I'll teach you!

01:07:23.520 --> 01:07:24.340
What?

01:07:26.910 --> 01:07:29.570
Wait, Your Highness!

01:07:29.570 --> 01:07:31.100
Please, stop!

01:07:34.040 --> 01:07:36.040
I can't, Your Highness!

01:08:05.320 --> 01:08:08.210
Let's get some sleep.

01:08:15.420 --> 01:08:16.630
Your Highness!

01:08:17.560 --> 01:08:19.470
Are you all right?

01:09:38.320 --> 01:09:40.240
Um...

01:09:40.240 --> 01:09:41.030
Yes?

01:09:41.030 --> 01:09:44.640
About last night...

01:09:52.190 --> 01:09:55.100
We have some good cloud cover today.

01:09:55.920 --> 01:09:59.430
Let's take off for the last time.

01:10:02.610 --> 01:10:04.190
Okay.

01:10:26.850 --> 01:10:29.960
We should reach Scion Island by the afternoon.

01:10:29.960 --> 01:10:32.510
That's where we will go our separate ways.

01:10:33.470 --> 01:10:35.640
Are you okay with that?

01:10:37.470 --> 01:10:41.220
Right now, I'm only thinking about reaching our destination safely.

01:10:41.210 --> 01:10:45.470
The enemy fleet must still be out here somewhere.

01:10:45.470 --> 01:10:52.850
They must have sent out patrols, knowing we were hiding on one of these islands.

01:10:58.350 --> 01:10:59.790
Hey.

01:10:59.790 --> 01:11:01.070
Yes?

01:11:01.070 --> 01:11:03.370
Teach me how to fire the gun.

01:11:03.370 --> 01:11:06.700
I pulled the trigger the other day, but nothing happened.

01:11:06.700 --> 01:11:08.900
The safety must have been on, that's why.

01:11:08.910 --> 01:11:11.280
Huh? Where is it?

01:11:11.280 --> 01:11:13.190
On the left side.

01:11:15.390 --> 01:11:17.640
Oh, here it is.

01:11:19.930 --> 01:11:21.260
Now it'll fire?

01:11:21.260 --> 01:11:23.930
Well, yeah, but...

01:11:23.930 --> 01:11:26.420
You said we still have a chance, right?

01:11:29.510 --> 01:11:31.040
All right.

01:11:31.040 --> 01:11:33.660
I'll let you know when to shoot.

01:11:33.660 --> 01:11:35.780
Hitting your target will be tough,

01:11:35.780 --> 01:11:37.980
but just try to aim at them.

01:11:37.980 --> 01:11:39.060
Okay!

01:11:41.020 --> 01:11:45.320
But with all of these clouds around, I don't think we'll be-

01:11:49.610 --> 01:11:51.830
<i>They're nearby.</i>

01:11:51.830 --> 01:11:54.070
<i>Have they already encircled us?</i>

01:11:54.080 --> 01:11:55.540
Behind us, on the left!

01:12:06.760 --> 01:12:10.520
Seven ships below us, rising!

01:12:10.510 --> 01:12:11.890
I'll try to shake them off!

01:12:21.630 --> 01:12:22.930
Air cruisers?

01:12:38.020 --> 01:12:39.720
I'm turning on the over-boost!

01:13:23.640 --> 01:13:25.050
You did it!

01:13:25.050 --> 01:13:28.050
Once we're in the clouds, we can escape.

01:13:29.220 --> 01:13:32.210
I guess we're not in the clear yet.

01:13:39.050 --> 01:13:40.820
Only one plane?

01:13:48.550 --> 01:13:50.130
That's...

01:13:56.570 --> 01:13:57.930
What's he doing?

01:13:57.930 --> 01:14:00.420
He wants to duel me.

01:14:00.410 --> 01:14:03.710
It's the old Amatsuvian way of settling a score.

01:14:03.710 --> 01:14:06.330
Like the samurai used to.

01:14:06.330 --> 01:14:09.710
It's their best chance at bringing us down.

01:14:09.710 --> 01:14:15.220
One very skilled pilot is much harder to evade than several mediocre ones.

01:14:16.100 --> 01:14:18.130
So, what will you do?

01:14:19.220 --> 01:14:21.850
If we can run away, we'll be in the clear.

01:14:21.850 --> 01:14:22.470
Okay.

01:14:27.980 --> 01:14:29.770
Show me how good you are.

01:14:33.650 --> 01:14:36.320
It all comes down to this, Your Highness.

01:14:36.320 --> 01:14:39.030
He is a skilled fighter, but let's get past him together!

01:14:39.030 --> 01:14:41.430
Okay! Together!

01:15:12.830 --> 01:15:15.070
He's coming from our left!

01:15:20.040 --> 01:15:21.650
Why isn't he shooting at us?

01:15:21.650 --> 01:15:25.650
Until he's within range, he won't waste ammunition by firing.

01:15:34.710 --> 01:15:35.960
I can't lose...

01:15:54.510 --> 01:15:59.000
I can't lose! Not after coming this far!

01:15:59.000 --> 01:16:00.550
I believe in you.

01:16:01.860 --> 01:16:03.420
I believe in you!

01:16:14.950 --> 01:16:16.210
How about this?

01:16:52.250 --> 01:16:53.250
Damn it!

01:17:03.720 --> 01:17:06.600
That's it, keep coming. I'll show you my ace move.

01:17:19.080 --> 01:17:20.070
Now!

01:17:30.790 --> 01:17:31.920
I win.

01:18:03.890 --> 01:18:07.450
Fana!

01:18:44.180 --> 01:18:46.160
He's still flying.

01:18:46.150 --> 01:18:48.700
He may be an enemy, but he's really something.

01:18:52.200 --> 01:18:53.640
I lost.

01:18:53.620 --> 01:18:56.800
I didn't think she had it in her to fire.

01:19:08.500 --> 01:19:09.640
Let's go.

01:19:09.640 --> 01:19:10.720
Okay!

01:19:54.620 --> 01:19:57.010
This is the end of our journey.

01:19:57.010 --> 01:20:00.270
We just have to wait for your pick-up to come from the mainland.

01:20:08.740 --> 01:20:12.270
I wish I could take her with me.

01:20:12.270 --> 01:20:16.270
It feels like I've become close friends with her.

01:20:16.270 --> 01:20:19.820
You can call yourself a pilot now, Your Highness.

01:20:20.740 --> 01:20:25.520
To us pilots, planes are part of our lives forever.

01:20:25.520 --> 01:20:28.070
Me? A pilot?

01:20:28.070 --> 01:20:30.240
You did defeat the enemy, after all.

01:20:30.240 --> 01:20:31.650
That makes you one.

01:20:32.490 --> 01:20:34.510
Only because you told me to.

01:20:35.470 --> 01:20:38.390
Didn't you call out my name?

01:20:38.390 --> 01:20:40.690
<i>Fana!</i>

01:20:41.230 --> 01:20:45.690
Oh, well, I thought we were goners...

01:20:49.890 --> 01:20:51.150
Really?

01:20:51.150 --> 01:20:52.830
I'm sorry.

01:20:54.750 --> 01:20:57.690
I was finally useful, wasn't I?

01:21:07.220 --> 01:21:09.860
Come to the capital with me.

01:21:11.270 --> 01:21:13.340
They won't allow that.

01:21:14.550 --> 01:21:17.640
That's just not right.

01:21:18.580 --> 01:21:21.570
They can't let it get out that it was a mercenary,

01:21:21.570 --> 01:21:24.280
not the Special Fleet, that escorted Your Highness.

01:21:24.280 --> 01:21:29.120
Then at least come on the ship with me and join in on the celebrations!

01:21:29.110 --> 01:21:30.150
Please!

01:21:30.150 --> 01:21:33.930
I wouldn't get my reward then.

01:21:37.370 --> 01:21:39.490
Didn't you say it wasn't about the money?!

01:21:40.650 --> 01:21:44.300
Mercenaries work for money.

01:21:44.300 --> 01:21:46.520
That's who I am.

01:21:46.500 --> 01:21:47.540
You're lying!

01:21:47.540 --> 01:21:48.920
No, I'm not!

01:21:51.020 --> 01:21:55.170
Then, you're saying you don't care if you never see me again?!

01:22:28.710 --> 01:22:31.480
That's some pick-up.

01:22:38.970 --> 01:22:43.480
They will most likely forbid me from stepping onto that ship.

01:23:20.390 --> 01:23:22.240
Please, look at me.

01:23:26.020 --> 01:23:30.770
I pray that your future be filled with nothing but happiness.

01:23:30.770 --> 01:23:35.200
I didn't bring us here by myself.

01:23:35.200 --> 01:23:37.790
We made it because you were right there behind me.

01:23:42.780 --> 01:23:45.270
Me too.

01:23:45.270 --> 01:23:47.370
If you weren't there with me...

01:23:52.330 --> 01:23:54.700
You are my hope.

01:23:54.710 --> 01:23:56.670
You always will be.

01:24:11.140 --> 01:24:11.960
Get away from her!

01:24:32.330 --> 01:24:34.960
Know your place, you filthy rat!

01:24:34.960 --> 01:24:35.730
No!

01:24:37.210 --> 01:24:39.260
What are you doing?!

01:24:39.260 --> 01:24:40.570
Please, step back.

01:24:42.420 --> 01:24:43.580
This way.

01:24:44.220 --> 01:24:46.400
Stop! What are you doing?

01:24:45.930 --> 01:24:46.930
Come.

01:24:46.400 --> 01:24:47.730
Let me go!

01:24:47.710 --> 01:24:49.240
I want to be with Charles!

01:24:53.360 --> 01:24:55.610
Check the amount.

01:24:56.520 --> 01:24:58.150
Hurry up!

01:25:07.970 --> 01:25:09.380
Let's see.

01:25:16.790 --> 01:25:18.740
You're set for life.

01:25:18.760 --> 01:25:22.720
I won't repeat what I saw back there. You should thank me.

01:25:22.720 --> 01:25:27.920
If the truth came out, you'd be shot dead on the spot.

01:25:28.710 --> 01:25:29.950
Let me go!

01:25:29.950 --> 01:25:31.720
Let him come, too!

01:25:31.720 --> 01:25:33.800
Charles, look up!

01:25:33.800 --> 01:25:35.720
Why are you kneeling down?

01:25:35.720 --> 01:25:38.270
You did things no one else could!

01:25:37.520 --> 01:25:38.270
Let's go.

01:25:38.270 --> 01:25:41.250
These guys are nothing compared to you!

01:25:41.870 --> 01:25:43.970
Say something, Charles!

01:25:44.560 --> 01:25:47.650
Charles!

01:26:50.650 --> 01:26:52.770
You were too cruel to him!

01:26:53.510 --> 01:26:56.130
Is this what the proud Levamme Kingdom does?

01:26:57.270 --> 01:27:00.280
He risked his life to bring me here!

01:27:00.270 --> 01:27:04.360
But you rewarded him like he was a dog!

01:27:04.360 --> 01:27:06.300
Do you think that's humane?!

01:27:06.300 --> 01:27:09.340
Your Highness, please calm down.

01:27:13.120 --> 01:27:18.040
It would seem that Her Highness has been deceived by that pilot.

01:27:19.290 --> 01:27:24.510
It's possible that in front of
Her Highness, he put on an air of nobility.

01:27:24.510 --> 01:27:29.310
But once that gold was in front of him, he couldn't hide his mercenary greed.

01:27:29.310 --> 01:27:34.250
When I looked back at him, he was ecstatic, drooling over his reward.

01:27:34.250 --> 01:27:37.210
I wish you could have seen him.

01:27:46.440 --> 01:27:48.070
Is that...

01:27:56.470 --> 01:27:58.390
It's the Santa Cruz!

01:28:00.100 --> 01:28:01.330
Charles!

01:28:01.330 --> 01:28:03.720
What's he thinking?!

01:28:07.850 --> 01:28:09.430
Please let me say goodbye!

01:28:09.430 --> 01:28:10.930
I don't think so.

01:28:10.930 --> 01:28:13.890
We can't have you going around and causing any misunderstandings.

01:28:13.890 --> 01:28:17.150
Why am I not allowed to say goodbye to the man who saved my life?

01:28:17.140 --> 01:28:21.980
Is the next queen going to bring
shame to her family once again?

01:28:28.490 --> 01:28:29.500
Move.

01:28:30.630 --> 01:28:32.910
Let me through!

01:28:32.910 --> 01:28:35.000
Is that an order?

01:28:34.990 --> 01:28:41.580
Until you marry the prince, you have no such power.

01:28:41.580 --> 01:28:47.670
You don't want to start off on the wrong foot, do you?

01:28:49.510 --> 01:28:52.140
Now, come quietly-

01:28:52.140 --> 01:28:54.160
Step back.

01:29:14.280 --> 01:29:17.050
No, wait. This isn't...

01:29:25.640 --> 01:29:27.660
Let her through.

01:29:40.600 --> 01:29:42.100
<i>Fana...</i>

01:29:51.710 --> 01:29:52.970
Sorry!

01:30:12.940 --> 01:30:15.830
Charles! Charles!

01:30:15.830 --> 01:30:17.040
Charles!

01:31:32.360 --> 01:31:34.090
Charles is dancing!

01:31:36.330 --> 01:31:38.380
Charles!

01:33:02.940 --> 01:33:05.680
Thank you, Charles!

01:33:05.680 --> 01:33:07.430
Thank you!

01:35:18.480 --> 01:35:24.050
yume no naka wo terase yo

01:35:18.480 --> 01:35:24.050
Illuminate the depths of your dream

01:35:24.050 --> 01:35:29.500
inishie no hoshiakari

01:35:24.050 --> 01:35:29.500
With history's starlight.

01:35:29.500 --> 01:35:34.880
yoru no umi wa utau yo

01:35:29.500 --> 01:35:34.880
While the sea sings at night,

01:35:34.880 --> 01:35:40.470
nemure nemure shizuka ni

01:35:34.880 --> 01:35:40.470
Rest your head quietly.

01:35:40.470 --> 01:35:45.850
yasuragi no naka de

01:35:40.470 --> 01:35:45.850
Stay within the reach of tranquility

01:35:45.850 --> 01:35:51.340
kanashimi ga hateru made

01:35:45.850 --> 01:35:51.340
Until your sadness fades away.

01:35:51.340 --> 01:35:56.760
ima dake me wo tojite

01:35:51.340 --> 01:35:56.760
Close your eyes for just a moment,

01:35:56.760 --> 01:36:03.490
kono mune ni mi wo makasete

01:35:56.760 --> 01:36:03.490
And give yourself to me.

01:36:06.240 --> 01:36:11.730
toki no naka wo nagaruru

01:36:06.240 --> 01:36:11.730
While time continues its endless flow,

01:36:11.730 --> 01:36:17.000
ikusen no kaze no koe

01:36:11.730 --> 01:36:17.000
The voice of a thousand gusts of wind

01:36:17.000 --> 01:36:22.550
sono uta wa tokoshie ni

01:36:17.000 --> 01:36:22.550
Will carry that song to eternity,

01:36:22.550 --> 01:36:27.970
susume susume to hibiku

01:36:22.550 --> 01:36:27.970
And let it echo forever

01:36:27.970 --> 01:36:33.530
mukou ni no naka de

01:36:27.970 --> 01:36:33.530
Within their midst

01:36:33.530 --> 01:36:39.140
kanashimi ga hateru made

01:36:33.530 --> 01:36:39.140
Until your sadness fades away.

01:36:39.140 --> 01:36:44.400
ima dake me wo tojite

01:36:39.140 --> 01:36:44.400
Close your eyes for just a moment,

01:36:44.400 --> 01:36:51.580
kono mune ni mi wo makasete

01:36:44.400 --> 01:36:51.580
And give yourself to me.

01:36:53.400 --> 01:36:58.930
hitomi wo hiraku toki

01:36:53.400 --> 01:36:58.930
And then, after opening your eyes,

01:36:58.930 --> 01:37:04.500
soko ni wana ni ga aru no darou

01:36:58.930 --> 01:37:04.500
Temptation will lie before you.

01:37:04.500 --> 01:37:09.890
ashita wo te ni suru toki

01:37:04.500 --> 01:37:09.890
Once you grasp tomorrow in your hands,

01:37:09.890 --> 01:37:15.900
soko ni wana ni ga aru no darou

01:37:09.890 --> 01:37:15.900
Temptation will lie before you.

01:37:15.900 --> 01:37:21.810
ano hi no shikai ga

01:37:15.900 --> 01:37:21.810
The entire world from back then

01:37:21.810 --> 01:37:26.600
itsuka kayou you ni

01:37:21.810 --> 01:37:26.600
Will one day sing that song.

01:37:26.600 --> 01:37:32.310
hikari wo machiwabite

01:37:26.600 --> 01:37:32.310
By then, the light will have tired of waiting,

01:37:32.310 --> 01:37:37.590
yami wo

01:37:32.310 --> 01:37:37.590
And will overcome

01:37:37.590 --> 01:37:42.710
koeru

01:37:37.590 --> 01:37:42.710
The darkness.

01:38:07.800 --> 01:38:13.650
takanatte yuku kodou no

01:38:07.800 --> 01:38:13.650
Our hearts are beating fast,

01:38:14.510 --> 01:38:18.590
oto wo kiitara

01:38:14.510 --> 01:38:18.590
And once we hear that song,

01:38:18.590 --> 01:38:23.870
tabidatsu kara

01:38:18.590 --> 01:38:23.870
Our journey will begin.

01:38:23.870 --> 01:38:29.420
shiroi tsubasa de

01:38:23.870 --> 01:38:29.420
We'll fly on white wings.

01:38:29.420 --> 01:38:35.250
kimi to dare no ga mirai e

01:38:29.420 --> 01:38:35.250
You will turn towards the future with another,

01:38:36.200 --> 01:38:45.790
mukau tabibito ano sora e to

01:38:36.200 --> 01:38:45.790
And journey into that open sky,

01:38:45.790 --> 01:38:52.630
tsubasa hirogete

01:38:45.790 --> 01:38:52.630
While spreading your wings.
